target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestFingerprint'
expect: Fingerprint =
why:    the agent figure is the SUM of the cycle rows' `agents`, not the number of cycles. Both are small integers that look plausible beside each other, so a report rendered from the wrong one reads fine — and the forgery resistance the fingerprint buys comes entirely from the numbers being derivable only from the record.
--- old
		fmt.Sprintf("%d cycle(s) · %d agent(s)", len(r.Cycles), r.AgentsSpent())}
--- new
		fmt.Sprintf("%d cycle(s) · %d agent(s)", len(r.Cycles), len(r.Cycles))}
